Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "FallingObjectInRainyConditions" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :vehicle1 ;
    :hasObstacle :roadObject1 ;
    :hasEvidence :fallingObject1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :rainy1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle .
:roadObject1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Hay bale falling/rolling onto the road" .
:fallingObject1 a :FallingObjectIndicator ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1 .
:rainy1 a :RainyCondition .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "High risk of collision with a falling object on a wet road surface" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 ;
    :confidenceScore "0.95"^^xsd:float .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .

Identified Risks for each risk class
Risk 1:
Description: Collision risk due to a falling object (hay bale) entering the vehicle's path in rainy, low-visibility conditions.
Severity Score: 0.90